net loan charge-offs, predominantly in the office portfolio, and higher commercial and industrial net loan charge-offs. The consumer net loan charge-off rate increased to 0.75% (annualized), up from 0.73%, on higher credit card and auto net loan charge-offs</font></div><div style="padding-left:9pt;text-indent:-9pt"><font style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#141414;font-family:'Wells Fargo Sans',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">&#9702;</font><font style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Wells Fargo Sans',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:5.59pt">Nonperforming assets as a percentage of total loans were </font><font style="color:#000000;font-family:'Wells Fargo Sans',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">0.86%, up 3 basis points</font><font style="background-color:#ffffff;color:#000000;font-family:'Wells Fargo Sans',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">, driven by higher commercial real estate and commercial and industrial nonaccrual loans, partially offset by lower residential mortgage nonaccrual loans</font></div><div style="height:36pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div style="text-align:center"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"></td><td style="width:32.233%"></td><td style="width:0.1%"></td><td style="width:1.0%"></td><td style="width:32.233%"></td><td style="width:0.1%"></td><td style="width:1.0%"></td><td style="width:32.234%"></td><td style="width:0.1%"></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><div><font style="color:#000000;font-family:'Wells Fargo Sans',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">Endnotes are presented on page 9.</font></div></td><td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vert